Date: Thu, 23 Sep 93 23:27:45 GMT
From: sjw@liberty.demon.co.uk (Stephen J. Whitrow)
Subject: Dark Matter Paradox Resolved!

A newspaper article I read yesterday makes me think that Klaus! was right
after all in his post of June 2nd on the Fermi Paradox.  Wednesday's
article states that some of the missing 'dark matter' (90% of the
universe's mass), has recently been identified at the edge of the Milky
Way.  An excerpt: "It is made up of huge invisible dark lumps, perhaps
comprising gaping black holes, or billions of objects the size of Jupiter."  

Some observational evidence was provided by a joint American-Australian
team based in Canberra, running a computer analysis of pictures taken
with a 125-year-old telescope, looking for stars which had glowed more
than usual.  They found one that had become 7 times brighter for 34 days.
A French team, at a laboratory outside Paris, recorded two star
magnifications.  The theory is that a dark lump or 'Macho' -- Massive
Astronomical Compact Halo Object -- temporarily passed in front of each
star, acting as a lens and magnifying its glow.  Although it was pointed
out that more examples would be needed for confirmation.  And the
headline was *Macho masters of the universe*.

Billions of objects the size of Jupiter?  Masters of the universe?  It
looks like we could be too late -- the lawyers have already taken control
of 90% of the matter in the universe!  I propose that one of the natural
laws that is written in the stars is the concept of 'tick'.  Some
epistemologies espoused by aliens suggest that it is not worth
distinguishing between the concept of an arachnid lifeform, the ticking
off that aliens keep receiving from their Jovian brain masters for any
failure to treat the masters as monarchs or for any feeble attempt to
win 'rights', the sound occuring at regular intervals as the lawyers
guzzle up more of their slaves' planets in order to expand, and the
'tick-tack' signals transmitted between lawyers as they announce the
odds each is prepared to lay on how many von Neumann probes he can eat
before breakfast.  Hence as the spontaneous order that we know as
'language' arose, it was in part predetermined by the thoughts of
aliens.  And in a great many races all four concepts came to be
represented by the same word (or with a brief suffix tacked onto it).

It's also quite possible that some of the dark matter is actually blue
goo.  The nano-Gorts are designed to extend each lawyer's rule of law
to the serfs, to prevent these mere serfs from getting a share of the
action, and allocating the 90% of the universe so far claimed in an
equal distribution between each lawyer.  Of course, each Jupiter brain
lawyer has produced many smaller humanoid units, living in the Dyson
spheres, and communicating with the central unit.  But the bad news is
that we Earthlings may be restricted to 10% of the universe, so that
everyone's share is only 10^-11 universes, an order of magnitude less
than previously assumed. 

ANNOUNCING A BET:  I wager $20 (or U.K. pounds) that no one will pay
me $10,000 for 10% of my rights to the universe, whether 10^-12 or
10^-11 universes (depending on the truth of the lawyer theory),
during the period that the bet is in force.

